Step 7 — Test API Gateway → Lambda

PURPOSE:
Why?
We're proving the complete flow works:
HTTP Request
     ↓
API Gateway
     ↓
Lambda
     ↓
Response

HANDSON:
In API Gateway, copy your Invoke URL.
It should look like:
https://xxxxx.execute-api.ap-south-1.amazonaws.com/dev

Add /devices:
https://xxxxx.execute-api.ap-south-1.amazonaws.com/dev/devices

Since you're on Windows, easiest is PowerShell:
Invoke-RestMethod `
  -Uri "YOUR_URL/devices" `
  -Method POST `
  -ContentType "application/json" `
  -Body '{"deviceId":"device-001","temperature":28}'
USE curl command in cmd:
curl -X POST "https://dworj763qg.execute-api.ap-south-1.amazonaws.com/dev/devices" -H "Content-Type: application/json" -d "{\"deviceId\":\"device-001\",\"temperature\":28}"

Expected response
message
-------
Hello from Lambda

Note:
Invoke-RestMethod → PowerShell command
curl → works from CMD
